<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal C/A deficit 423.7 bln esc in Jan-May.</title>
<headline>Portugal C/A deficit 423.7 bln esc in Jan-May.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal had an accumulated current account deficit of 423.7 billion escudos between January and May after a deficit of 500.6 billion in the same period of 1996, the Bank of Portugal said.</p>
<p>Figures in billions of escudos:</p>
<p>			 Jan-May 97  Jan-May 96	 May 97    May 96</p>
<p>    C/A balance     -423.7	 -500.6	   -106.6    -93.2</p>
<p>    Goods	     -820.7	 -749.8	   -173.6    -147.6</p>
<p>    Services	    5.9	    -5.5	     12.1     0.6</p>
<p>Foreign investment</p>
<p>    in Portugal	369.4	   513.8	    81.3    201.3</p>
<p>Portuguese investment</p>
<p>    abroad	     -230.2	  -568.6	   43.7   -54.7</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
